<title>UK: Brunner Mond shares make dull debut.</title>
<headline>Brunner Mond shares make dull debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Brunner Mond Plc made a dull debut in the market on Thursday, trading at 171p by 1216 GMT compared with a price of 175p at which they were placed with institutional investors.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the soda ash producer said the stock had suffered by making its debut on the same day as AEA Technology, which traded at a strong premium.</p>
<p>&quot;It was offered with a dividend yield of just under 6.0 percent in compensation for lower growth and had blue chip support,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
</text>
